# Zombie Echo - Design Changes

While developing Zombie Echo, I made a few changes to my original game design as I worked on the gameplay and tested different features.

**Weapons and Ammo**

Originally, I planned for the player to start with a pistol that had limited ammunition. I changed this so the pistol has unlimited reserve ammo, allowing the player to always have a weapon available. I also added a system that automatically switches the player back to the pistol when the shotgun or assault rifle runs out of ammo.

Instead of having weapons randomly spawn around the arena, I changed it so zombies have a chance to drop a shotgun or assault rifle when they die.

**Pickups**

I added a timer to the health, ammo, and weapon pickups so they disappear after 7 seconds if the player doesn't collect them. This encourages the player to move around the arena instead of staying in one place.

**Walls and Vision**

I added walls and obstacles to the arena to make movement and positioning more important. I also changed the flashlight and shooting cones so they stop when they reach a wall instead of going through it. Bullets are also blocked by walls, preventing the player from shooting zombies through obstacles.

**Weapon Balancing**

I adjusted the damage, range, firing speed, and ammunition for each weapon while testing the game. The shotgun deals more damage but has a shorter range, while the assault rifle shoots faster and has a longer range. The pistol remains the default weapon.

**Zombie Difficulty**

I added a wave system where more zombies spawn as the player progresses. Zombie movement speed also increases as the waves go on, making the game more difficult over time.

**Audio and Animations**

I added background music and different gunshot sounds for the pistol, shotgun, and assault rifle. I also added different player appearances depending on the equipped weapon, along with reload animations.

Overall, these changes were made to improve the gameplay, balance the weapons, and make surviving the zombie waves more challenging.
